# errcheck exclusions — functions whose returned error is genuinely nothing to act on.
#
# Everything NOT listed here must have its error handled. The gate exists
# because a discarded gorm error is invisible: the statement fails, the value
# stays zero, the request answers 200. Two live bugs shipped that way
# (galgame.user_id, galgame_website_tag_relation.tag_id).
#
# Add an entry only when the error cannot be acted on, and say why.

# Deferred reader/closer cleanup — the read already happened.
(io.Closer).Close
(*os.File).Close
(io.ReadCloser).Close
(*database/sql.Rows).Close

# Response writers: the connection is already gone if these fail.
(net/http.ResponseWriter).Write

# goldmark's BufWriter wraps a bufio.Writer over an in-memory buffer and its
# error is checked once at Flush, not per write.
(github.com/yuin/goldmark/util.BufWriter).Write
(github.com/yuin/goldmark/util.BufWriter).WriteByte
(github.com/yuin/goldmark/util.BufWriter).WriteString
